lert service to auto-update the CMDB has webhook url without credentials in the azure portal","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sys_kb_id=1bf707c5938fe550d9743f986cba10b9","line":26},{"title":"Cloud User portal","target":"cloudmgt-cloud-user-portal","line":30},{"title":"Cloud Provisioning and Governance","target":"cloud-management-v2-landing-page","line":47},{"title":"Azure alert driven discovery with reader privileges","target":"https://community.servicenow.com/community?id=community_article&sys_id=32edaa41db2fa090679499ead39619a1","line":81},{"title":"KB0963526","target":"https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB0963526","line":104},{"title":"Add an Azure service account","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/cloud-configuration-governance/azure-service-account-cloud-mgt.md","line":140},{"title":"Supported Microsoft Azure alert types","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-operations-management/discovery/microsoft-azure-alert-driven-discovery.md","line":184},{"title":"Microsoft Azure","target":"https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/?product=popular","line":218},{"title":"Discovery","target":"r-discovery","line":279},{"title":"Azure change processing","target":"azure-change-processing","line":280},{"title":"Service Mapping","target":"c_ServiceMappingOverview","line":281},{"title":"Cloud User Portal","target":"cloudmgt-cloud-user-portal","line":282},{"title":"Cloud Provisioning and Governance","target":"cloud-management-v2-landing-page","line":283}],"metadata":{"title":"Microsoft Azure Alert driven discovery","description":"The Microsoft Azure Alert service can raise alerts for any changes in the life-cycle state or the configuration of a cloud resource. You can configure the service to auto-update the latest resource information in the Configuration Management Database \\(CMDB\\) without waiting for the next scheduled Cloud Discovery to run. Configure the Microsoft Azure Alert service to auto-update the Configuration Management Database \\(CMDB\\) without waiting for the next scheduled Cloud Discovery to run.Enable alert-driven discovery for a new Microsoft Azure alert type by adding it to the Azure Alert Rules \\[azure\\_alert\\_rule\\] table.The base system Cloud Discovery supports alert driven discovery for several Microsoft Azure alert types. The Azure Alert Rules \\[azure\\_alert\\_rule\\] table contains the supported alert types.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-operations-management/discovery/microsoft-azure-alert-driven-discovery.html","release":"australia","product":"Discovery","classification":"discovery","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":6,"breadcrumb":["Discovery for Microsoft Azure","Discovery for cloud environment","Discovery","ITOM Visibility","IT Operations Management"],"tags":["#it-operations-management","#discovery","#cmdb","#patterns","#ci","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[61,79],[110,112],[238,275]],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/it-operations-management/discovery/microsoft-azure-alert-driven-discovery.md"},
